    "body": "The repository has no `Example` functions, so the pkg.go.dev pages show signatures without usage. Examples are compiled and run by `go test`, so they also act as tests.\n\n## What to add\n\nOne `Example...` function per package, in `example_test.go` (package `<name>_test`), with an `// Output:` comment so it is verified:\n\n- `pkg/chain`: write a few events to a `JSONLChain` and print the `seq`/`prev_hash` linkage (print only stable values, for example the sequence numbers and whether `prev_hash` of event 2 equals the hash of line 1).\n- `pkg/govdecision`: `GenerateEd25519`, sign a decision, verify it, then show verification failing after the message is altered.\n- `pkg/spool`: `Open` a file spool in `t.TempDir()`-style temp dir (use `os.MkdirTemp` in the example), `Enqueue`, then `Reconcile` into a `SinkFunc`.\n- `pkg/resilient`: a breaker or backoff usage with a deterministic clock (see `clock.go`).\n- `pkg/identity`, `pkg/cryptoprofile`: a short example each.\n\nYou do not need to cover every package in one PR. Keep each example under about 25 lines and deterministic (no wall-clock or random values in the output).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `go test -race ./...` passes; `go vet ./...` clean.\n- Standard library only (the module has no third-party dependencies; keep it that way).\n- Commits signed off (`git commit -s`); see CONTRIBUTING.md.\n\nEstimated size: S.\n",
